  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile models dominate (0.59–0.65), with scvi_n200 consistently outperforming pca_n2000, and image-only models are very weak (0.21). Aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) has minimal impact (~0.003). Uncertainty: We have not tested scgpt, the third available RNA encoder, and it is unclear whether it can match or exceed scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting. This experiment (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, acc=0.650), isolating the encoder effect while holding profile and aggregation constant. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, it opens a new high-performing direction for subsequent multimodal experiments; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the best encoder and can redirect budget toward testing whether multimodal fusion or a stronger image encoder (ViT) adds value. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves a key untested design axis at the current performance frontier without conflating multiple changes."
